From: tao3k team and Contributors
Subject: [CANDIDATE] gambit: propagate Darwin macro tracking policy to bootstrap

Apply after 0004. Bootstrap configures an unpatched release archive with
C_COMPILER, not FLAGS_OBJ_DYN. Put the existing capability-probed option on
the inherited compiler command so both the current tree and archive receive
it. The existing Darwin/GNU/non-LLVM guard and optimization policy remain.
This candidate has no new performance admission and is not in the release stack.

diff --git a/configure b/configure
--- a/configure
+++ b/configure
@@ -12705,3 +12705,5 @@
              if test "$C_COMP_LLVM" != yes; then
-               FLAGS_OBJ_DYN="$FLAGS_OBJ_DYN$DASH_ftrack_macro_expansion_0"
+               # Bootstrap forwards C_COMPILER to the unpatched archive.
+               # Keep this probed option on that inherited command too.
+               C_COMPILER="$C_COMPILER$DASH_ftrack_macro_expansion_0"
              fi
diff --git a/configure.ac b/configure.ac
--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -2585,3 +2585,5 @@
              if test "$C_COMP_LLVM" != yes; then
-               FLAGS_OBJ_DYN="$FLAGS_OBJ_DYN$DASH_ftrack_macro_expansion_0"
+               # Bootstrap forwards C_COMPILER to the unpatched archive.
+               # Keep this probed option on that inherited command too.
+               C_COMPILER="$C_COMPILER$DASH_ftrack_macro_expansion_0"
              fi
